over the years batman has more than  earned his place in pop culture legend  and for more reasons than one he boasts  a remarkable rogues gallery he's a key  player in super teams like the justice  league and he's a merchandising  juggernaut to boot and of course you  can't ignore arguably the most important  aspects of batman's iconic appeal the  bat suit as long as there's been a  batman there's been a bat suit in some  form or fashion some are cloth and some  are rubber some are armored and some are  lightweight they come in a range of  color schemes ear and cape lengths and  utility belt sizes regardless of the  specifics though batman rarely leaves  the batcave without one his suits go a  long way in keeping him safe and they  help strike beer into the hearts of  gotham city's criminals what gives you  the right what's the difference between  you and me i'm not wearing hockey pads  still as badass as many of batman's  costumes may be the truth is they're far  from perfect and if you place them into  a real world context some serious issues  begin to present themselves arguably one  of the most glaring problems has even  been examined by physicists who  explained why a bat suit wouldn't work  in real life as it does in the comics  cartoons or movies any batman fan will  tell you that most bat suits are  incomplete without a cape after all they  don't call him the caped crusader for  nothing on the surface the cape seems  like little more than an aesthetic  choice but in truth many batman  incarnations have used it for much more  than looking good aside from using it as  a means of intimidation against gotham  criminals it has often been used as a  method of gliding across large distances  and while this may look cool on the  silver screen or in the pages of a comic  book the truth is that this function  isn't nearly as plausible in reality  back in 2012 physicists at the  university of leicester published a  study in the journal of special physics  topics it read clearly gliding using a  bat cape is not a safe way to travel  unless a method to rapidly slow down is  used such as a parachute they noted that  after leaping from a 150 meter high  gotham city skyscraper batman could  realistically glide for approximately  350 meters on a 4.7 meter wingspan  before the velocity levels off at 110  kilometers per hour at that point an 80  kilometer per hour descent would begin  causing the dc comics mainstay to  plummet to his death unless he found  something to break his fall still  there's nothing wrong with pretending  that batman can use his cape to glide  from building to building it's a fun  mechanic to use in the batman arkham  video games for example and it sets up  some neat visuals on the big screen but  there's one other aspect of the suit  that's even less practical than the cape  a cowl specifically those worn by the  likes of michael keaton and his  successors for their live-action movie  appearances seeing as these specific  cowls consisted of one solid piece from  the shoulders up it would be incredibly  difficult for batman to turn his head in  fact this has even caused problems  during filming on batman movies in the  past at a 2014 press event michael  keaton discussed his struggles with the  headpiece while filming 1989's batman  revealing that moving his head at the  neck was next to impossible as a result  he had no choice but to move his entire  upper body for moments in which batman  had to turn and look in a different  direction that's obviously inconvenient  for an actor let alone someone trying to  fight off two or three bad guys at once  from cape to cowl the batsuit is  something of a mess by real world  standards and it's typically presented  as the ultimate suit of armor at the  cinema on tv and in the pages of dc  comics at the end of the day though  suspension of disbelief is the name of  the game with stuff like this as long as  it looks cool that's all that really  matters  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

